A||||1||SUPERDUTY TT FIERO||what tire and rim size can fit on a stock fiero???||||6||
Z||000000||SUPERDUTY TT FIERO||12-28-2001||12:33 PM||||i have a 1986 fiero se 2.5 liter and currently i have 16" chrome helo jewel rims 16"x7" and with 205/45/zr16 tires on it i want the largest that i can fit ive heared that 18" can fit on the rear and 17" can fit on the front with no modifications to the struts, but what tire size can fit? i want to get a 17x 7.5 on thr front and a 18x8 on the rear with 225/40 17 in the front and 255/40 18 on the rear is that possible or is it farfetched?? thanks and if anyone wants to purchase the old 16"rims the style is evolution and look great on a fiero and im selling them for 800 rim and tire<P>thanks||||reg||6
Z||000001||artherd||12-29-2001||01:34 AM||||On an 88 those would fit, but on an 87 I think you'll have rubbing if you go any higher than:<P>17x7 40mm front 215/45/17<BR>18x8 (40-50mm) rear with 235/45/18 (or 245/40/17 MAYBE... not on all wheels.)<P>NOTE: you can upgrade to an 88 rear cradle!  THis will allow you to run your 18x8.5 with 255/40/18 rears  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The fronts will be fine at 215/45/17, that's all the more you want up there anyway.  anything more is a waste, just makes the car hard to turn.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red.                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver, In-Progreess.                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
